menu "T-Dongle DOOM hardware modes"

config TD_USB_HOST
    bool "Enable native USB host keyboard controls"
    default n
    help
        Switch GPIO19/GPIO20 to USB-OTG host mode and accept boot-protocol
        keyboards. This disconnects USB Serial/JTAG at runtime. Use only with
        a current-limited externally powered host adapter; the T-Dongle-S3
        cannot safely source keyboard VBUS by itself.

config TD_AUDIO_PDM
    bool "Enable eight-channel PDM sound-effects output"
    depends on !TD_USB_HOST
    default n
    help
        Mix the ADPCM sound effects already stored in the WHD image and send
        22.05 kHz mono audio through the ESP32-S3 PCM-to-PDM converter. GPIO43
        is PDM clock and GPIO44 is PDM data on the Qwiic connector. The data
        signal requires an external low-pass filter and audio amplifier.

config TD_WEB_AUDIO
    bool "Enable synchronized browser sound and music events"
    depends on !TD_AUDIO_PDM
    default y
    help
        Preserve DOOM's native eight-channel sound semantics and music state,
        but send compact events to the Wi-Fi control deck for Web Audio
        playback. The renderer never streams or mixes PCM on the ESP32.

endmenu
